<title>USA: Texas Instruments, Lockheed Martin get contract.</title>
<headline>Texas Instruments, Lockheed Martin get contract.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A joint venture formed by Texas Instruments and Lockheed Martin Corp was awarded a $192-million portion of a fixed-price, multi-year weapons contract, the Defense Department said on Friday.</p>
<p>The multi-year contract has a cumulative total of $745 million for full-rate production of the JAVELIN Weapon system.</p>
</text>
